<< /A << /BBox [ 63.4394 471.572 531.439 761.443 ] /O /Layout >> /Alt (Neural network architecture illustrating the proposed multilayer perceptron model. The input layer contains eight encoded features grouped into numeric variables \(study hours and prior course experience\), ordinal variables \(GPA level and engagement level\), and one-hot encoded assessment types \(fill in the blanks, multiple choice, short answer, and true or false\). These inputs connect to a single hidden layer with sixteen fully connected neurons using ReLU activation, L2 regularization, and dropout. The output layer contains three Softmax neurons that classify anticipated assessment difficulty into Easy, Moderate, or Hard.) /K 14 /Lang (en-EN) /P 316 0 R /Pg 195 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
